<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>Operation Vantage, 1961</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; June 25th 1961 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Persian Gulf &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United Kingdom &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The unpredictable Abdul Karim Qasim seized power in Iraq in 1958, un-stabilizing the region. In 1961, following Britain's withdrawal from Kuwait, Qasim unilaterally announced that Kuwait was to be considered Iraqi territory and would be incorporated into Iraq as their 19th Province. The British Government had given Kuwait assurances of military support in the event of an attack on their territory. So when the newly independent state called for protection, British air, sea and land forces were in place within days in a urgent military operation codenamed Operation Vantage. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
